From: Qualcomm upstream backport
Subject: [PATCH] soc: qcom: socinfo: add SoC ID 498 (QCS6490)

Mainline knows QCM6490 (497) but not QCS6490 (498), which is what this SoM
reports. socinfo_machine() then returns NULL and /sys/devices/soc0/machine
falls back to the device-tree model string ("8devices Robonode Vision"
etc.) instead of the chip name.

That breaks anything keying off the SoC identity. Concretely, Qualcomm's
userspace-resource-manager selects its per-target policy by lowercasing
soc0/machine and matching "qcs6490", so on these boards it silently applies
no tuning at all - while the QLI 2.0 reference, whose kernel carries these
two commits, applies the qcm6490 policy correctly.

Squashed backport of the two upstream commits, taken verbatim from
qcom-6.18.y:
  7d8563688866 dt-bindings: arm: qcom,ids: Add SoC ID for QCS6490
  2baf0be6a28d soc: qcom: socinfo: Add SoC ID for QCS6490

Upstream-Status: Backport

diff --git a/include/dt-bindings/arm/qcom,ids.h b/include/dt-bindings/arm/qcom,ids.h
index 19598ed4679e..8776844e0eeb 100644
--- a/include/dt-bindings/arm/qcom,ids.h
+++ b/include/dt-bindings/arm/qcom,ids.h
@@ -240,6 +240,7 @@
 #define QCOM_ID_SC7280			487
 #define QCOM_ID_SC7180P			495
 #define QCOM_ID_QCM6490			497
+#define QCOM_ID_QCS6490			498
 #define QCOM_ID_SM7325P			499
 #define QCOM_ID_IPQ5000			503
 #define QCOM_ID_IPQ0509			504
diff --git a/drivers/soc/qcom/socinfo.c b/drivers/soc/qcom/socinfo.c
index a2e2e15b840c..704235ad9ccf 100644
--- a/drivers/soc/qcom/socinfo.c
+++ b/drivers/soc/qcom/socinfo.c
@@ -415,6 +415,7 @@ static const struct soc_id soc_id[] = {
 	{ qcom_board_id(SC7280) },
 	{ qcom_board_id(SC7180P) },
 	{ qcom_board_id(QCM6490) },
+	{ qcom_board_id(QCS6490) },
 	{ qcom_board_id(SM7325P) },
 	{ qcom_board_id(IPQ5000) },
 	{ qcom_board_id(IPQ0509) },
